Z||000020||firstfiero||09-28-2001||01:39 PM||||     They talked about it on the Today show yesterday. Two reasons they pointed out why it's fake. 1)From the direction it's coming it would be the first hit on a tower. Their is know observation deck on that tower. The observation deck is on the 2nd tower that was hit. 2) Anybody notice that the guy is dressed for winter on a hot summer day. I<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Ken Wittlief||09-28-2001||04:39 PM||||the photo from the roof reminds me of something that happened when I was there back in May of this year.<P>When you walk around the top and look down you cant help but wonder - if I jump - how long will it take to reach the bottom.<P>Since I took physics in college it was easy to figure out in my head - a skydiver falls at 200mph = 300 feet per second.<P>  so you would fall for roughly 5 seconds. It seems morbid now - but after I had already figured this out I overheard a couple of other people, standing by the edge, and they were wondering the same thing and trying to take a guess at it.<P> I think I said it before on another thread - walking around up there on the observation roof, and knowing how long it would take to get down the stairs - i definately had an uneasy feeling being up there - like simply being there was taking a risk.||||reg||10
Z||000022||Ken Wittlief||09-28-2001||08:39 PM||||was thinking about this on the drive home - assuming terminal velocity like a skydiver was oversimplifying - it takes about 10 seconds to reach terminal velocity<P> have to use the X=0.5AT^2 equation instead.<P>comes out closer to 9 seconds.||||reg||1
Z||000023||My7Fieros||10-15-2001||08:54 PM||||Yeah its def a fake...got an email the other day w/ that pic and pics of that guy on the Titanic, the Hindenberg, the bus from "Speed" you name it.||||reg||1
